# Pricing

Choosing the right price is an important part of successfully selling products on the Codexeron Marketplace.

This guide explains how pricing works and provides recommendations for setting fair and competitive prices.

---

# Overview

Product pricing should reflect:

- Product quality
- Features
- Complexity
- Support commitment
- Update frequency
- Market demand

Sellers are responsible for setting and maintaining their product prices.

---

# Pricing Guidelines

When determining a price, consider:

- Development time
- Product quality
- Documentation quality
- Long-term maintenance
- Customer support
- Competitor pricing

Choose a price that accurately reflects the value of your product.

---

# Free Products

The availability of free products depends on current marketplace policies.

If supported, free products must meet the same quality standards as paid products.

---

# Price Changes

Sellers may update product prices when necessary.

Price changes do not affect completed purchases.

Customers who purchased a product before a price change retain access according to their license terms.

---

# Discounts and Promotions

Promotional campaigns may be available through marketplace features.

When available, sellers should ensure promotional pricing is clear and accurate.

---

# Refund Considerations

Pricing should take into account the marketplace refund policy.

Products should accurately represent their features to reduce refund requests.

---

# Best Practices

To improve customer confidence:

- Set realistic prices.
- Keep pricing consistent.
- Avoid misleading discounts.
- Update prices only when justified.
- Deliver value that matches the product price.

